WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-VI

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:09.920
Hello.  Welcome back
to Lam Rim.

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:14.080
Today we will review the
entire course.

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:18.000
That's good for me.  I also want to review the material.

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:22.000
By working through these individual modules

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:26.000
and then studying them at separate times,

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:28.240
you're essentially losing the flow of the entire lesson.

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:32.040
I was thinking it would be great today
if we could go back to the

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:36.040
beginning and go through the entire circuit of the

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:38.720
Lam Rim lecture that we had.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:44.120
I will implement that circuit based on the IDIMs,
on the concept images,

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:49.040
that we use to teach ACI teachers.

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:50.640
ACI teachers

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:54.120
are expected to be able to look at
one of these images

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:57.960
and recognize the idea behind it.

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:00.600
I think, Tim, we were talking about how many there would be?   A thousand or something like that?

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:04.120
How much?

00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:10.160
500, or something like that.
Therefore, it's quite easy to conduct a test

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:13.960
to examine someone based solely on
pictures.

00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:15.560
Therefore, we are only
posting these pictures for you.

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:19.120
So, I'm going to challenge you throughout this review session:

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:21.680
when we show you a picture,

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:25.400
I'll give you a second to see if you

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:28.000
can remember what the picture is about.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:29.400
Okay, and this is a pretty good review

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:33.960
of the entire course we're doing.
Okay, let's begin.  The

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:38.040
first picture, Sejii,

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:43.400
is meant to remind you

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:48.880
that we are in the midst of practices

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:51.800
for people of average ability,

00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:53.920
and what they are trying to achieve is Nirvana.

00:01:54.040 --> 00:02:00.200
They are trying to escape the Wheel of Samsara, to
escape their own suffering.

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:04.040
This is where the Buddha taught three practices

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:08.520
that will help you attain
your personal Nirvana.

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:13.880
The third training is understanding emptiness,
understanding the pen.  The

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:17.240
second form of training is meditation.

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:22.600
On a deeper level, both of these practices
can only be done in a quiet place,

00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:28.240
during specific times of the day, when you are truly focused on your meditation cushion.

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:33.080
To a deeper level, both of these exercises
must be performed

00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:36.200
at specific times of the day.

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:41.040
But this training, the foundation of those two trainings, is treating others with kindness.

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:42.720
You could call it morality.

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:45.200
You could call it an ethical way of life,

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:50.120
but ultimately, it's about treating
other people kindly.

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:52.200
That's the foundation,

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:55.160
something that's always available to us throughout the day.

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:59.240
This is one of the three extraordinary practices
of Buddhism,

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:02.160
serving as a means to help us attain Nirvana.

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:05.440
And this is available to us throughout the day.

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:06.800
So in this picture,

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:11.800
you can see Sejii helping
Geshe Michael figure out what's going on with his computer.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:16.160
That is one of the kindest things
young people can do for older people.

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:22.320
Look at the next picture; can you remember
what it is?  Have

00:03:26.440 --> 00:03:28.440
