That's a real sorcerer."

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:04.240
Or perhaps you're thinking of the old picture
of Nagarjuna,

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:08.080
and he, he was completely kind of mystical.

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:12.320
In Lam Rim, what we learned

00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:15.280
is that this woman

00:04:16.120 --> 00:04:18.920
has several children, she is married,

00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:23.480
and she is a sorceress.
She is a true sorceress.

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:28.920
Pabongka Rinpoche said, don't think that a Dharma Master has to sit on a throne and

00:04:29.480 --> 00:04:32.160
recite certain Tantric rituals.

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:35.320
What is this woman doing?

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:39.080
She is paying her taxes.  Being

00:04:40.040 --> 00:04:44.200
honest with your tax money seems to be
really difficult in my country.  It

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:47.760
can take you weeks to
file your taxes

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:50.240
and to do them really carefully,

00:04:50.440 --> 00:04:52.440
to do them completely honestly,

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:55.080
to pay every single penny that you owe.

00:04:55.840 --> 00:04:57.840
This led her...

00:04:57.960 --> 00:05:02.160
She received the first of the extraordinary trainings of a good person;  Be

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:04.240
kind to others.

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:06.840
That makes her a true sorceress.

00:05:06.840 --> 00:05:11.280
Forget the pictures you have of Lamas
wearing large hats

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:13.000
and ringing bells.
Okay, that's easy.

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:14.880
Anyone can do that.

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:18.040
Being kind to others is difficult,

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:21.480
and maintaining your morals,
upholding your ethical standards, is

00:05:22.120 --> 00:05:23.440
also difficult.  The

00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:26.000
next picture;

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:31.480
I'll give you a moment.
Do you remember what this is about?

00:05:35.840 --> 00:05:40.680
The quote in Lam Rim is
TSUL KHRIMS LDAN PA'I DGE SLONG 'OD DANG LDAN:

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:44.040
A person who is truly upholding
their vows,

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:48.040
truly upholding the principles of Buddhism,
especially the Ten Principles,

00:05:48.040 --> 00:05:51.000
they shine, they truly shine.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:06:00.160
A person who is making a healthy, humble, simple effort to keep their commitments,

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:02.800
to maintain good karma and be

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:05.400
kind to others,

00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:09.000
they seem to have a certain peace
on their face;

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:11.560
they are radiating.

00:06:11.560 --> 00:06:13.680
When they walk into a room,
you know it.

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:18.800
Everyone started to feel better, just
like Tim and Sejii.

00:06:19.800 --> 00:06:21.200
It is a light of the world.

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:24.680
The Buddha said, those people are the light
of the world.

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:27.840
There is a Christian saying;

00:06:28.040 --> 00:06:33.840
Don't put a candle under a basket; let the world see your happy faces.

00:06:34.720 --> 00:06:41.320
And that is a true guiding light
for the whole world.

00:06:42.520 --> 00:06:44.920
The next picture, IDIM #4.

00:06:50.080 --> 00:06:59.080
This is a rock formation that I visited with my partner Veronica for her birthday during this Lam Rim course.

00:07:01.080 --> 00:07:08.320
They were talking about sunset,
which in Tibetan is called NUB PA.

00:07:08.320 --> 00:07:12.080
It is also a word for west
because the sun sets in the west;

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:13.960
NUB PA means

00:07:14.120 --> 00:07:17.480
the sun is setting, and it's a very sad verb.

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:22.160
This is a very sad idea in Buddhism,

00:07:22.320 --> 00:07:29.360
most famously found at the end of Abhidharma kosha, The Treasure House of Higher Wisdom.

00:07:29.360 --> 00:07:33.080
The Treasure
House of Higher Knowledge, written by
Vasubandhu, states:

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:40.440
"The sun of the Dharma, the light of the Dharma,
will set on this world."

00:07:40.440 --> 00:07:44.920
We will lose the light of France in this world.  The world will descend into darkness.

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:47.000
After a certain period of time,

00:07:47.760 --> 00:07:51.040
the teachings of the Buddha will disappear
from this world.

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:57.440
First, they will fade from people's minds, but they will still remain in libraries.

00:07:57.440 --> 00:08:01.160
Those books are still in the libraries.  It is possible that these are libraries that John Brady has not yet found.

00:08:01.760 --> 00:08:05.680
And then they will disappear from the libraries,
and then they will vanish.

00:08:08.120 --> 00:08:13.200
I put this picture here because Papongka Rinpoche made a special point; he said,

00:08:14.600 --> 00:08:21.000
"If you cannot keep your commitments, if you cannot maintain a kind attitude towards
others,

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:24.160
then we can say that the Dharma
has left this world."

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:27.760
The light of France has left this world
within you.

00:08:28.440 --> 00:08:32.120
The sun has set inside
your own chests, and

00:08:32.120 --> 00:08:35.920
it would be very sad if we did not keep our vows.  The

00:08:36.040 --> 00:08:38.040
next picture.

00:08:44.720 --> 00:08:49.600
We call this the "Love and
Compassion in the Time of the Virus" retreat.  The

00:08:50.920 --> 00:08:56.920
main point is that during
that very difficult time in the world,

00:08:57.080 --> 00:08:59.080
if you kept your commitments,

00:08:59.080 --> 00:09:02.200
if you were kind to others

00:09:02.440 --> 00:09:05.760
when things were scary and frightening
and the virus was spreading.

00:09:05.760 --> 00:09:07.560
We don't know where,
we don't know how,

00:09:08.120 --> 00:09:10.240
and we don't know how many
people will die.

00:09:11.400 --> 00:09:18.160
If, during those difficult times,
you do something kind for others,

00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:20.560
it will be so much more powerful.

00:09:20.800 --> 00:09:23.880
He mentioned, if you remember,
a 5-star Buddhist paradise.

00:09:24.600 --> 00:09:27.080
It's like a perfect place.

00:09:27.840 --> 00:09:31.200
It's easy to be a good person;
everyone there is a good person.

00:09:32.040 --> 00:09:34.680
That's not a great achievement.
It's not a big deal,

00:09:34.680 --> 00:09:36.640
and the seeds aren't that strong

00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:40.080
to be kind in a group of kind people.

00:09:40.240 --> 00:09:44.240
Be kind when people are attacking you,
when everyone is afraid.

00:09:45.200 --> 00:09:49.000
When people aren't being kind to each other,
and to be someone who

00:09:49.960 --> 00:09:55.440
stands up and shares things during
these difficult times –

00:09:55.560 --> 00:09:58.800
that's an extremely pure person.

00:09:59.000 --> 00:10:02.960
That was a great achievement.  That's an
incredible karma, far more powerful.

00:10:02.960 --> 00:10:05.200
I think this virus is a very good time,

00:10:06.040 --> 00:10:10.520
and it's a great opportunity for all of us
to prove

00:10:10.720 --> 00:10:15.840
whether we are truly Buddhists.
And are we truly practicing the
Bodhisattva Path?

00:10:15.840 --> 00:10:20.040
Can we help others
even when things are so difficult?  The

00:10:20.960 --> 00:10:22.960
next picture.

