00:11:57.560 --> 00:12:02.120
into more languages ​​or anything like
that.  That was a very important French influence.

00:12:02.920 --> 00:12:06.680
But he said, if you spread it
in your own heart,

00:12:07.280 --> 00:12:11.280
then of course it will spread outward because the world is coming from your heart,

00:12:11.280 --> 00:12:13.000
really from your Heart Chakra.

00:12:13.760 --> 00:12:18.200
The next picture is number 7.

00:12:20.720 --> 00:12:24.720
Try to remember what this picture is about.
I'll give you a second.

00:12:29.960 --> 00:12:33.000
This is one of my favorite topics;  to

00:12:33.680 --> 00:12:43.400
have a personal relationship with another person,
just like these two people have.

00:12:45.080 --> 00:12:49.200
In my opinion, and in Tantra, it is one of the happiest things that can happen to you.

00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:53.200
It's one of the greatest things that
could happen to you guys.

00:12:54.120 --> 00:12:59.000
Anyone can tell you why the whole world is looking for a life partner,

00:12:59.840 --> 00:13:01.480
that it makes people happy.

00:13:01.480 --> 00:13:04.720
It's one of the greatest joys
when things go well.

00:13:05.840 --> 00:13:09.000
It's one of the greatest joys
you can have, but

00:13:09.840 --> 00:13:14.120
you know, and I know, when it doesn't go well,

00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:17.560
it's one of the greatest sorrows
in life.

00:13:18.320 --> 00:13:21.200
Why is that relevant to this course
right here?

00:13:25.200 --> 00:13:30.520
If your morals are good,

00:13:30.720 --> 00:13:32.800
that is the greatest happiness in
your life.

00:13:33.400 --> 00:13:38.440
And if you break your morals,
that's what will make you miserable.

00:13:38.680 --> 00:13:41.760
It's like having a kind woman or man as your life partner, the

00:13:42.720 --> 00:13:46.120
same person who can make you
completely happy, but

00:13:46.160 --> 00:13:49.200
can also make you completely miserable.

00:13:49.720 --> 00:13:53.840
So in this case, the Law,
your personal practice of kindness,

00:13:54.320 --> 00:13:57.680
good behavior, is being compared to
a life partner who

00:13:57.680 --> 00:14:01.120
could or will create the best


00:14:01.760 --> 00:14:04.760
or the worst thing in your life—the
same person.

00:14:05.440 --> 00:14:11.520
Next IDIM, number 8.

00:14:12.920 --> 00:14:15.200
This is a complex image.
Let's see if you can remember!

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:19.000
I'm going to have a drink of my green beverage.

00:14:20.160 --> 00:14:22.160
Thank you, Vimala.

00:14:30.920 --> 00:14:35.040
This really represents a breach of
your commitments.

00:14:35.440 --> 00:14:41.040
Pulling out a weed represents breaking
your commitments.

00:14:41.080 --> 00:14:46.680
Why would destroying this tree be considered a breach of
your commitment?

00:14:46.920 --> 00:14:53.040
If you're a gardener,
you know that you should remove weeds

00:14:53.920 --> 00:14:56.160
before the seeds are ready.

00:14:56.880 --> 00:15:00.920
If you wait until the seeds
are ready to fall,

00:15:01.360 --> 00:15:03.280
and then you pull out the weeds,

00:15:03.560 --> 00:15:06.040
you will have sown about a thousand seeds.

00:15:07.000 --> 00:15:12.680
In the next month or year, you will have thousands of weeds growing back.

00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:14.920
Therefore, you must attack
those weeds as soon as possible.

00:15:15.960 --> 00:15:20.560
This relates to a very radical statement

00:15:20.800 --> 00:15:22.800
that the Buddha made:

00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:29.240
DGE SLONG DAG SROG DANG BRAL ZHING
SHI BA NI BLA'I.  I would rather

00:15:29.680 --> 00:15:31.680
die

00:15:31.760 --> 00:15:33.960
than break your vows.
Why?

00:15:35.000 --> 00:15:37.000
When you break your vows,

00:15:37.080 --> 00:15:40.360
you are scattering seeds

00:15:40.520 --> 00:15:44.160
that will continue to fall for many lifetimes.

00:15:44.720 --> 00:15:51.080
If you die, you will destroy
a mind-body complex.

00:15:51.960 --> 00:15:55.440
If you die, you will destroy
a very useful shrine,

00:15:55.440 --> 00:15:58.800
a physical shrine and a mind.
You only lose one.

00:16:00.040 --> 00:16:02.040
But if you break your commitments,

00:16:02.720 --> 00:16:05.920
you will lose many complex mind-body relationships.

00:16:05.920 --> 00:16:08.920
You have ruined your body and mind
over many lifetimes.

00:16:09.680 --> 00:16:12.920
And just as you are scattering seeds

00:16:12.920 --> 00:16:15.720
that will destroy many lives.

00:16:15.800 --> 00:16:21.880
The Buddha said;  He would rather die than break
your vows, and

00:16:22.080 --> 00:16:28.920
he was not speaking in parables.
He was speaking literally

00:16:28.920 --> 00:16:32.720
when he said that.  I would rather die than break
my promises.

00:16:34.800 --> 00:16:36.800
There's a joke in Lam Rim.

00:16:38.240 --> 00:16:45.760
We take a vow never to abandon
Bodhicitta, even if it means sacrificing
our lives.

00:16:48.040 --> 00:16:53.960
There's a famous saying, "
All our lives we're waiting

00:16:54.040 --> 00:16:56.040
to be thrown into prison

00:16:56.240 --> 00:16:58.240
by some evil person."

00:16:58.600 --> 00:17:03.960
They come up to us, hold a knife to our throats, and say, “Give up
your Bodhisattva vows or die today.”

00:17:04.520 --> 00:17:06.120
Then we say,

00:17:06.120 --> 00:17:07.960
“I choose to die.”

00:17:07.960 --> 00:17:10.600
And they kill us.

00:17:11.080 --> 00:17:14.720
I think we’ve all been waiting for this since
we took those vows.

00:17:15.560 --> 00:17:19.720
We’ve all been waiting for these people to show up
with knives and threaten us.

00:17:19.720 --> 00:17:24.320
But we are the ones holding the knives.
We threaten our Bodhisattva vows
every day.

00:17:26.000 --> 00:17:33.200
We have to make this decision every day when we decide whether or not to keep our vows
carefully.

00:17:36.280 --> 00:17:39.200
It’s hard to find those people who
throw you in jail and say, “

00:17:39.440 --> 00:17:42.920
I will kill you if you don’t give up
your Bodhisattva vows.”

00:17:46.040 --> 00:17:48.040
The next picture.

